---
description: Docker, compose, env, entrypoints, production deploy
globs: "docker-compose*.yml,Dockerfile*,docker/**,.env*,start-dev-services.sh,Makefile,scripts/**/*.sh"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Infra

- Local deps: `./start-dev-services.sh` (or `make up`) — app on host via `devserver`. Script exit / Ctrl+C / terminal close → `compose down` (volumes kept unless `--clean`).
- Bind mounts live under `./volumes/<service>/` (postgres, redis, rabbitmq, …); data is gitignored via `.gitkeep` placeholders.
- Prod: `docker-compose.yml` + entrypoints under `docker/`.
- Deploy version: Docker `ARG VERSION` → `/app/version.txt` → public `GET /api/v1/versions/` (`config/deploy_version.py`). Pass `VERSION=` on compose/CI image builds.
- Dev entrypoint / `devserver`: migrate + `seed_demo_data` (local admin) — see `commands` rule.
- New/changed env → update `.env.example` and document production defaults.
- Broker/cache/DB/port/volume/healthcheck changes → developer alert section required (see `core` rule).
{%- if cookiecutter.use_i18n == "y" %}
- i18n: `LANGUAGE_CODE` in `.env`; catalogs via `make translations` — see `i18n` rule.
{%- endif %}
{%- if cookiecutter.use_otp_login == "y" %}
- OTP: `OTP_TEST` (+ optional `SMS_PROVIDER` / TTL env) — see `otp-auth` rule.
{%- endif %}
{%- if cookiecutter.use_google_login == "y" or cookiecutter.use_microsoft_login == "y" or cookiecutter.use_apple_login == "y" %}
- Social OAuth client IDs in `.env` / `config/settings/social_auth.py` — see `social-auth` rule.
{%- endif %}
{%- if cookiecutter.use_rabbitmq == "y" %}
- RabbitMQ 4+: keep `docker/rabbitmq/rabbitmq.conf` (`transient_nonexcl_queues` permit) — Celery needs it.
{%- endif %}
{%- if cookiecutter.use_celery == "y" %}
- Celery worker/beat: compose services + `scripts/run_celery_*.sh` / entrypoints.
{%- endif %}
{%- if cookiecutter.reverse_proxy == "nginx" %}
- Reverse proxy: Nginx (`docker/nginx/`).
{%- elif cookiecutter.reverse_proxy == "traefik" %}
- Reverse proxy: Traefik (`docker/traefik/`).
{%- endif %}
- Changing infra/env patterns → update **this rule file** in the **same** change.

